},{"id":"sec_s1l5_concept","type":"rule_paragraph","data":{"text":"<div class=\"lesson-concept-svg\" style=\"margin:14px 0;padding:12px;border-radius:12px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a,#1e293b);border:1px solid #334155;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 760 190\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"u123grad\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#0d9488\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#0284c7\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"744\" height=\"174\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#0f172a\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"22\" y=\"20\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" fill=\"url(#u123grad)\"/>\n  <text x=\"97\" y=\"37\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">UNIT 1 • LESSON 5</text>\n  <text x=\"188\" y=\"38\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Aham Qur'ani Asmaa (Set 5 — A'maal wa Jaza) (Page 22–23)</text>\n  <rect x=\"24\" y=\"58\" width=\"220\" height=\"68\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#1e293b\" stroke=\"#475569\"/>\n  <text x=\"134\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" direction=\"rtl\" font-family=\"Traditional Arabic,Amiri,serif\">الْأَجْرُ ، النِّعْمَةُ</text>\n  <circle cx=\"288\" cy=\"92\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#0d9488\"/>\n  <text x=\"288\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Qur'ani Alfaaz (Set 5)</text>\n  <rect x=\"332\" y=\"58\" width=\"402\" height=\"68\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0f292a\" stroke=\"#14b8a6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"533\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"23\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" direction=\"rtl\" font-family=\"Traditional Arabic,Amiri,serif\">الْأَجْرُ ، الْمَغْفِرَةُ ، التَّقْوَىٰ ، الزَّلْزَلَةُ</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"150\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• الْأَجْرُ ، النِّعْمَةُ (Ajr, Ne'mat) → الْأَجْرُ ، الْمَغْفِرَةُ ، التَّقْوَىٰ ، الزَّلْزَلَةُ (Badla, Bakhshish, Parhezgari, Zalzalah).</text>\n  <text x=\"26\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">• Unit 1 mein aasaan Qur'ani alfaaz aur buniyadi ishaare/qawa'id sikhaye gaye hain.</text>\n</svg>\n</div>\n**Qaa'ida (Pages 22–23):** Is sabaq mein ajr, maghfirat, taqwa aur aakhirat se muta'alliq 36 aham Qur'ani asmaa aur 12 Qur'ani aayatein shamil hain."}},{"id":"sec_s1l5_lbl0","type":"section_label","data":{"text":"Darj zail Qur'ani alfaaz ke ma'ani aam taur par aap jaante honge. Nisbatan naye alfaaz ke ma'ani unke saath de diye gaye hain. Faraham karda jagahon mein inke matlab likhein:"}},{"id":"sec_s1l5_g1","type":"two_col_numbered_list","data":{"is_numbered":false,"items":[{"id":"s1l5_g1_w1","arabic":"الْأَجْر","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">الْأَجْر</span>","hinglish":"Ajr / Sawaab / in'aam","translations":{"en":"Reward / Recompense","ur":"اجر / ثواب / انعام","hi":"अज्र / सवाब / इनाम"}},{"id":"s1l5_g1_w2","arabic":"الْبَيْت","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">الْبَيْت</span>","hinglish":"Ghar","translations":{"en":"The House","ur":"گھر / بیت","hi":"घर"}},{"id":"s1l5_g1_w3","arabic":"الْخَوْف","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">الْخَوْف</span>","hinglish":"Dar / Khawf","translations":{"en":"Fear","ur":"ڈر / خوف","hi":"डर / ख़ौफ़"}},{"id":"s1l5_g1_w4","arabic":"الْمِسْكِين","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">الْمِسْكِين</span>","hinglish":"Miskeen / Gareeb","translations":{"en":"Poor / Needy","ur":"مسکین / غریب","hi":"मिस्कीन / ग़रीब"}},{"id":"s1l5_g1_w5","arabic":"الْعَالِم","arabic_markup":"<span class=\"arabic-root\">الْعَالِم</span>","hinglish":"Aalim / Jaanne wala","translations":{"en":"The Scholar / The Learned (Knower)","ur":"عالم / جاننے والا","hi":"आलिम / जानने वाला"}},{"id":"s1l5_g1_w6","arabic":"الْوَزْن","arabic_mark